Z||000000||theogre||05-30-2000||01:12 AM||||Sorry guys & gals, I haven't forgotten to finish the updates I started some weeks ago when I put the test tunnel up for review.<P>I've been recovering from some minor injuries that make it dificult to sit at the computer for long periods of time. (My left leg is up on the desk as I write this. Slightly awkward....) Plus now Cliff is on holliday and I don't want to pester him with single page updates.<P>Since the test appeared to go well, I'm updating everything that was already there and adding numerous new pages.<P>Some of the new/updated things:<P>A sensor Quick Reference Guide.<BR>Some things to do when looking for vacuum leaks in a fiero.<BR>My experience converting to power windows. As soon as I'm able to finish the project. the inside wiring is done but I can't put the doors on for at least a couple more weeks. (The one thing, in addition to tilt wheel, that should be standard in all fiero.)<BR>some more MVAC notes.<BR>additional door info.<BR>updates to the power trunk latch pages.<BR>and some notes about a problem with 86.5+ 4 cyl automatics and the problem these have with the dog bone.||||reg||9
